cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Synlexa Studio"
message: "If you use Synlexa Studio in research or software, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
version: "0.4.5"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Yali"
    given-names: "Atil"
    alias: "nanobiolog"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Synlexa/synlexa-studio"
url: "https://www.synlexa.com"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, offline-capable structural biology, peptide biophysics, CRISPR/transcriptomics,
  and small-molecule cheminformatics workbench powered by a zero-dependency pure-Rust core
  (synlexa-bio-core), WebAssembly ABI v1, C++20 reference library, Python/TypeScript SDKs,
  local MCP server, and optional self-hosted GPU compute bridge.
  For research and development use. Not for diagnostic or treatment decisions.
keywords:
  - computational-biology
  - structural-bioinformatics
  - kabsch-superposition
  - cheminformatics
  - webassembly
  - mcp
  - research-software
